---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions - DiabeMate"
  description="Terms and Conditions and Medical Disclaimer for DiabeMate - Personal health and blood sugar logging companion."
>
  <main class="min-h-screen px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <header class="border-b border-surface-border pb-8">
        <div class="inline-block px-3 py-1 mb-4 text-xs font-mono font-semibold tracking-wider uppercase rounded-full bg-accent-primary/10 text-accent-primary">
          DiabeMate Legal
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text-primary">
          Terms &amp; Conditions
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-text-secondary">
          Last updated: October 2026
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="space-y-8 text-text-secondary leading-relaxed">
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary">1. Important Medical Disclaimer</h2>
          <p>
            DiabeMate is designed solely as a personal self-management tracking tool and informational companion for healthy lifestyle routines. DiabeMate is <strong>NOT a medical device (Software as a Medical Device / SaMD)</strong>, diagnostic system, or automated clinical decision service. This application does not diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease, illness, or medical condition.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary">2. No Medical Advice or Medication Dosage Calculations</h2>
          <p>
            DiabeMate will never calculate, recommend, or adjust prescription medication or insulin dosages. Never alter your insulin units, prescribed medications, dietary regimens, or physical activity limits without the express guidance and direct supervision of a licensed physician or qualified healthcare professional.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary">3. Apple Health &amp; Health Connect Integration</h2>
          <p>
            Integration with Apple Health or Google Health Connect is provided purely for your personal self-monitoring convenience. Users remain responsible for verifying the accuracy of third-party synced readings originating from smartwatches, continuous glucose monitors (CGM), or smart scales.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary">4. Emergency Medical Situations</h2>
          <p>
            If you experience severe hypoglycemia (&lt; 70 mg/dL), severe hyperglycemia (&gt; 250 mg/dL), ketones, shortness of breath, confusion, or any critical medical symptoms, immediately follow your clinician-provided emergency action plan or contact emergency medical services (such as 112 / 119 / 911 or your local emergency department).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary">5. User Responsibility &amp; Data Accuracy</h2>
          <p>
            You are solely responsible for verifying the accuracy of all values logged and for making informed health decisions in direct consultation with your healthcare provider. Any patterns or trends shown in the Insights engine are automated mathematical observations and do not represent clinical causation.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary">6. In-App Purchases and Subscriptions</h2>
          <p>
            Certain advanced features (such as 90-day clinical reports and custom theme palettes) may require a Pro subscription. Subscriptions are billed through Apple App Store or Google Play Store and can be managed or canceled anytime in your store account settings.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary">7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p>
            The application is provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo; without warranty of any kind. Under no circumstances shall DiabeMate, its creators, or contributors be held liable for any health decisions, adverse events, or outcomes resulting from the use of or reliance upon this software.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-text-primary">8. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>
            If you have questions regarding these Terms &amp; Conditions, please contact us via our developer support channel or official listing contact.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
